ce is an unordered frozenset.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["signing.py:115 `OPCERT_KINDS = frozenset({...})` (unordered)","jobs.py:38 and remote_cert.py:24 are ordered tuples","app.py:222 `detail\": f\"kind must be one of {list(jobs.VALID_KINDS)}\"`","certs.py:51 `choices=remote_cert._VALID_KINDS`","_USAGE current text is ordered: `{completion-verifier|plan-review}`"],"finding":"The chosen mechanism substitutes an unordered frozenset (OPCERT_KINDS) for ordered tuples, but two consumer sites render kinds into deterministic user-facing text: app.py:222 emits `list(jobs.VALID_KINDS)` in an error detail, and certs.py:51 feeds _VALID_KINDS to argparse `choices=` (help/error output). Iterating a frozenset gives no stable order, so error/usage text can vary run-to-run; AC2 mandates _USAGE be 'generated not re-typed' but never requires a deterministic order (e.g. sorted()).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd49d37e67cfc4ad4","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — generate-from-canonical; AC2","norm_id":"n4216d8dcdb40108d","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A user submits an invalid kind and the error `detail` lists kinds in a different order across processes","CLI --help / usage text order flips between runs"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Wrap canonical-set renderings in `sorted(...)` at the usage-string, app.py error-detail, and argparse choices sites so output order is stable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reac